Key changes:

- Atomic no-replace initial publication, preserving raced foreign destinations.
- Same `O_NOFOLLOW` descriptor used for archive hashing and bounded USTAR parsing.
- Correct descriptor cleanup on every injected `fdopen` failure.
- Added race, symlink, oversized metadata/archive, and descriptor-leak regressions.
- Updated [relay_asset_manifest.py](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/scripts/relay_asset_manifest.py), [test_relay_asset_manifest.py](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/scripts/tests/test_relay_asset_manifest.py), and [LOGBOOK.md](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/LOGBOOK.md).

All gates passed:

- 19 Python tests and 4 Swift manifest tests
- Deterministic accepted-archive regeneration
- Bundle/provider graph and unsigned Apple product validation
- Core and protocol gates
- Broad Swift suite: 450 tests, 25 existing known issues
- Black, Python compilation, and diff checks

The board outcome was updated and handoff exited `0`, status `to-review`. The validator still reports the pre-existing epic aggregate-status mismatch despite exiting `0`.
